# vulture allowlist — one identifier per line, or one line of
# `# type: ignore[unused]` pointing at an intentional false positive.
#
# vulture is a Python dead-code detector. It's noisy on any project
# with dynamic dispatch (Flask/Django views, pytest fixtures, entry
# points). The allowlist is how you tell it what's actually reachable.
#
# Common categories (uncomment + tune):

# — pytest fixtures + Django/Flask decorated views —
# fixture_*
# view_*
# api_*

# — CLI subcommand handlers auto-discovered by name —
# cmd_*

# — dunder methods sometimes flagged as unused —
# __init_subclass__
# __post_init__

# — SQLAlchemy / ORM columns referenced via string names —
# id
# created_at
# updated_at
